We present \ours{}, which embeds geometric safety awareness into a flow-matching VLA at training time with zero inference overhead. An auxiliary SDF head predicts signed distances from the model's internal representations, and a noise-aware collision-shaping loss penalizes near-collision trajectories. After training, the auxiliary head is discarded and the base $\pi_{0.5}$ policy is deployed unchanged (Figure~\ref{fig:overview}).


